<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How Yucca Homeware collects, uses and protects your personal information when you shop, book services or join a virtual class." active="privacy" draftNote="This policy should be reviewed and completed for your business and applicable Kenyan privacy obligations (Data Protection Act, 2019) before launch.">
  <p>We collect the details you provide when creating an account, placing an order, requesting a service, booking a consultation or virtual class, or contacting us. We use this information to respond to you and fulfil your request. Newsletter subscriptions are stored separately and can be removed by contacting us.</p>
  <h2>How information is used</h2>
  <p>Order, address and contact information is used to process purchases and communicate about delivery or service. Passwords are stored as secure hashes. Payment credentials are not stored by this site; M-Pesa payments are processed by Safaricom under its own privacy terms.</p>
  <h2>Virtual classes</h2>
  <p>When you book a class we use your name, email and phone number to confirm the booking and send the meeting link. Google Meet sessions are scheduled through Google Calendar, so your name and email are shared with Google for the invitation. Zoom and WhatsApp sessions are subject to those providers’ terms.</p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You may request access to, correction of or deletion of personal information, subject to records we must retain for legal or business purposes. Contact us using the details shown on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
